  "limitations": [
    "Native thread identity is11.95% slower in the first order and1.55% faster in reverse: no repeatable native thread win claimed.",
    "Opaque owned Go callback is0.39% and2.17% slower; its helper still executes in Go, and the full corpus remains required.",
    "Minimal dependent loop is unchanged in code size, minus0.56% / plus0.58% timing.",
    "Compact code grows1248 to1280bytes; native thread and minimal loop sizes are unchanged.",
    "Compiler cost includes default and explicit bounds; no allocation/code growth in those compile-only cohorts; source-specific adapter compile phases are captured separately.",
    "Source byte hashes can differ because generated helper addresses change between Go binaries; code-size equality alone is not instruction identity.",
    "No production deployment; local full-source publication pending complete audit."
  ]
